 857               
 858               /THIS SUBROUTINE TAKES THE INVERSE FFT (IFFT) OF THE DATA IN THE BUFFER.
 859               /IT IS ASSUMED THAT THIS DATA IS STORED IN SEQUENTIAL ORDER.
 860               /THE RESULTS ARE STORED IN BIT INVERTED ORDER.
 861               /THE ALGORITHM USED IS AS FOLLOWS:
 862               /       THE NORMAL TRANSFORM IS PERFORMED, EXCEPT:
 863               /       ON FETCHING THE VALUE FOR IM[W^K], WHICH IS 
 864               /       THE SIN(2*PI*K/N), THIS SIN VALUE IS NEGATED.
 865               /
 866               /THE REASONING FOR THIS IS AS FOLLOWS:
 867               /       A WEIGHTING FACTOR OF W^(-K) IS USED IN THE IFFT
 868               /       AND SINCE W^K AND W^(-K) ARE THE SAME EXCEPT THAT
 869               /       THEIR IMAGINARY PARTS HAVE OPPOSITE SIGNS, IT FOLLOWS
 870               /       THAT IM[W^K] SHOULD BE REPLACED BY -IM[W^K].
 871               
 872 010756  0000  IFFT,   0
 873 010757  7300          CLA CLL
 874 010760  1367          TAD CCIA        /NEGATE IM[W^K]. GET CIA INSTRUCTION
 875 010761  3766          DCA I SGNADJ    /AND PUT AT LOCATION ADJSGN.
 876 010762  4443          JMS I DOFFT     /DO FFT.
 877 010763  1370          TAD CNOP        /RE-INSTATE NOP AT ADJSGN FOR FFT.
 878 010764  3766          DCA I SGNADJ
 879 010765  5756          JMP I IFFT      /EXIT.
